# SAP extraction cron jobs.
# Times are in the server's timezone (EC2 default: UTC). 00:30 UTC = 06:00 IST.
# Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 failed, 2 partial, 75 skipped (previous run still running).
# Detailed log: /opt/sap-extraction-api/log/cron.log ; JSON result of each run: log/cron.out
#
# 1-minute delta sync (BSID, BSAD, VBRK, VBRP -> queue -> ingestion API).
# Normally installed by:  sudo DELTA_MODE=cron bash deploy/install.sh
# which writes it to /etc/cron.d/sap-extraction-delta (with the user column, as below) and
# disables the systemd worker. Use either this cron OR the worker, never both.
# --cron: each run polls SAP, checks / submits one ingestion job and exits (no waiting);
# a run that overlaps the previous one skips the parts still running (file locks).
# * * * * * sapapp /opt/sap-extraction-api/deploy/run_cron.sh delta --cron >> /opt/sap-extraction-api/log/cron.out 2>&1

# Optional - full loads of the non-delta [sap] tables (e.g. KNA1, T001) once a day at 06:00 IST.
# Not needed while [sap] tables only lists delta tables.  (crontab -e format: no user column)
# 30 0 * * * /opt/sap-extraction-api/deploy/run_cron.sh sync >> /opt/sap-extraction-api/log/cron.out 2>&1

# Fallback only - direct copy active_bsid -> active_bt3h while the ingestion API is not available.
# Remove it once the delta sync ingests BSID, otherwise invoices appear twice in active_bt3h.
# */5 * * * * /opt/sap-extraction-api/deploy/run_cron.sh sync-bt3i >> /opt/sap-extraction-api/log/cron.out 2>&1
